# Hot paths on x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, checked by `cargo xtask codegen check`.
# One function per line: its Rust path, then what the pinned toolchain's
# release build made of it. `asm` is a hash of the inline assembly's mnemonics
# and their count, `glue` the instructions the compiler generated around it,
# `calls` how many of those are calls. Rewrite the numbers with
# `cargo xtask codegen bless --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`.
# `body=compiler` marks a function whose assembly covers only part of it: the
# rest is intrinsics, exact on the pinned build and not bounded elsewhere.
